    <paragraph>For the following exercises, evaluate $$f(-3),f(2),f(-a),-f(a),f(a + h).$$</paragraph>
    <exercise number="27" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = 2x - 5$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$f(-3)=-11; f(-3)=-11;$$ $$f(2)=-1; f(2)=-1;$$ $$f(-a)=-2a-5; f(-a)=-2a-5;$$ $$-f(a)=-2a+5;-f(a)=-2a+5;$$ $$f(a+h)=2a+2h-5 f(a+h)=2a+2h-5$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
